Found in the k403 review: OTel records the tool start in plugin_before_tool_call keyed by name+args; if a later plugin skips or renames the call, the queued start stays and the next same-named call pops it. Limited to one iteration (_tool_starts resets per LLM call). Proper fix needs the tool call id in the hooks.

Tool hooks get optional trailing $call {id}; Plugin::OTel pairs tool spans by it via Hash::Util::FieldHash (stale starts vanish when the call is dropped). Tests t/94_plugin_otel_tool_call_ids.t, t/46_tool_hook_call_arg.t.

